NE Delta Fixes. 

!!!!! The NE Delta Board schematics and gerber were fixed but they have been not
verified yet !!!!!

#####   $C011 and $C012 IO   #####

$C011 address should contain the state of the selected $Dxxx bank on bit 7 of 
the response, while $C012 should contain information on the switch of the same 
address range between ROM and RAM.

In the DELTA, the responses for reads on addresses between $C010 - $C017 are
handled by IC63, a 74LS251. I1 of said IC is tied to VCC, I2 to GND, hardwiring 
the values for the two addresses.

Potential fix

   * Remove IC63 (74LS251) from its socket and bend pin 2 and 3 outward so they 
    don't make contact with the socket anymore
    
   * Solder a jumper wire from pin 5 of IC41 (74LS173) to pin 2 of IC63 (74LS251)
    
   * Solder a jumper wire from pin 3 of IC41 (74LS173) to pin 9 of IC5 (74LS04)
  
   * Solder a jumper wire from pin 8 of IC5 (74LS04) to pin 3 of IC63 (74LS251)
  
$Dxxx bank switching

The "Language card" style bank switching is handled by IC41 (74LS173) and 
IC42 (PLD). According to Jim Sather's Understanding the Apple IIe, enabling 
writes to the RAM bank in $Dxxx should work by having the /HRAMWRT signal reset,
which first requires having the PRE-WRITE signal to be set.

/HRAMWRT is reset by an odd read access in the $C08x range while PRE-WRITE is 
set. It can be set by any even access in the $C08x range. Any other type of 
access leaves the state of /HRAMWRT unchanged.

In the DELTA, IC41 and IC42 set the write enable signal only by checking that 
the access to the address is an odd one, and that the pre-write signal is 
enabled. They do not differentiate between reads or writes. So odd writes seems
to be able to reset the signal equivalent to /HRAMWRT when the pre-write is set
already.

#####   DHR   #####

In Apple IIe the DHR mode is activated with AN3. In NE Delta with AN2.

Potential fix

   * Just swap pins 11 and 12 of IC58 (74LS259)



